5: Lucas Guivera - Data Parsing, API Implementation (CRUD Endpoints)

1. Data Parsing

The goal of this component was to extract transaction data from the modified_sms_v2.xml file and convert it into a structured format that can be used by the API.

Key tasks completed:

Parsed the XML file using Python's xml.etree.ElementTree.
Read each SMS record and extracted relevant transaction information.
Classified SMS messages into transaction types such as incoming transfers, outgoing transfers, payments, airtime purchases, bank deposits, cash withdrawals, and reversals.
Used regular expressions to extract important fields including:
Transaction amount
Transaction fee
Account balance
Sender/receiver information
Transaction ID
Converted each SMS into a JSON-compatible dictionary.
Stored all records as a list of transaction objects that can be consumed by the REST API.

2. REST API Implementation (CRUD Endpoints)

The goal of this component was to expose the parsed transaction data through a REST API built using Python's http.server module.

Key features implemented:

Create (POST)
POST /transactions
Allows users to create a new transaction record.
Validates required fields before insertion.
Generates a unique transaction ID.
Returns the newly created transaction with HTTP 201 Created.
Read (GET)
GET /transactions
Retrieves all transaction records.
Supports pagination and filtering by transaction type.
GET /transactions/{id}
Retrieves a specific transaction using its ID.
Returns HTTP 404 if the transaction does not exist.
Update (PUT)
PUT /transactions/{id}
Updates an existing transaction.
Accepts JSON data containing the fields to be modified.
Returns the updated transaction.
Returns HTTP 404 if the record cannot be found.
Delete (DELETE)
DELETE /transactions/{id}
Removes a transaction from the dataset.
Returns a success message when deletion is completed.
Returns HTTP 404 if the transaction does not exist.
